{"total_count":1326,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/commits/46b20026392d0c98b45a0a1c96d75bd823353169","sha":"46b20026392d0c98b45a0a1c96d75bd823353169","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0NjU2MDA5NzU6NDZiMjAwMjYzOTJkMGM5OGI0NWEwYTFjOTZkNzViZDgyMzM1MzE2OQ==","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/46b20026392d0c98b45a0a1c96d75bd823353169","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/commits/46b20026392d0c98b45a0a1c96d75bd823353169/comments","commit":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/git/commits/46b20026392d0c98b45a0a1c96d75bd823353169","author":{"date":"2026-07-31T13:55:52.000-07:00","name":"Tristan Rice","email":"rice@fn.lc"},"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T01:57:48.000Z","name":"PyTorch MergeBot","email":"pytorchmergebot@users.noreply.github.com"},"message":"[c10d] Validate all-to-all split sizes (#191511)\n\nThe nccl2 all-to-all path cast split sizes directly to unsigned values and only normalized the case where both split lists were empty. Negative values wrapped and malformed lists reached NCCL. Gloo and stock NCCL also bypassed leading-dimension validation when both lists were empty, allowing equal splits that did not divide the tensor along dimension zero.\n\nApply the shared c10d split checks to every Gloo, stock NCCL, and nccl2 configuration before launch, and independently normalize empty nccl2 input and output split lists. This gives all three implementations the same validation and equal-split semantics.\n\nTest Plan:\n\n```bash\nBUILD_TEST=0 USE_FBGEMM=0 USE_NNPACK=0 USE_PYTORCH_QNNPACK=0 USE_QNNPACK=0 USE_XNNPACK=0 USE_FLASH_ATTENTION=0 USE_MEM_EFF_ATTENTION=0 USE_DISTRIBUTED=1 USE_CUDA=1 USE_NCCL=1 .venv/bin/pip install -e . -v --no-build-isolation\n```\n\n```bash\nNCCL_DEBUG=WARN NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=eth0 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 .venv/bin/python test/distributed/test_c10d_collectives.py GlooCollectivesTest.test_all_to_all_single_independent_empty_split_sizes GlooCollectivesTest.test_all_to_all_single_invalid_split_sizes NcclLegacyCollectivesTest.test_all_to_all_single_independent_empty_split_sizes NcclLegacyCollectivesTest.test_all_to_all_single_invalid_split_sizes Nccl2CollectivesTest.test_all_to_all_single_independent_empty_split_sizes Nccl2CollectivesTest.test_all_to_all_single_invalid_split_sizes -v\n```\n\n```bash\nspin lint\nlintrunner -a\n```\n\nAuthored with an AI assistant.\nPull Request resolved: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/191511\nApproved by: https://github.com/kapilsh, https://github.com/fduwjj\nghstack dependencies: #191510","tree":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/git/trees/69baf676a0c19fdad8bb44af4481c91d6bb74593","sha":"69baf676a0c19fdad8bb44af4481c91d6bb74593"},"comment_count":0},"author":{"login":"d4l3k","id":909104,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTEwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/909104?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k","html_url":"https://github.com/d4l3k","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d4l3k/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"pytorchmergebot","id":97764156,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdPDPA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97764156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytorchmergebot","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorchmergebot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytor